    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d244-f1" n="1" xml:id="d244-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed. For text of the Atomic Energy Act of 1946, Public Law 585, 79th
                    Congress, 2d Session, see 60 Stat. 755.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d244-f2" n="2" xml:id="d244-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d244-f3" n="3" xml:id="d244-f3-content">
                <p>In matters of atomic energy policy, President Truman frequently directed the
                    Secretary of State, the Secretary of Defense, and the Chairman of the United
                    States Atomic Energy Commission to constitute themselves as a Special Committee
                    of the National Security Council with a view to preparing recommendations for
                    the President.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
